            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0409" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/1573: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-12T17:00:00-04:00">July 12, 1940—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>263. Your 563, July 11, 9 p.m., and previous.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d427-f1"/> We
                    are giving careful study to your comments and suggestions in regard to the
                    problems presented by the present situation in American-Japanese relations. In
                    connection with this study we should like to have as soon as possible an
                    elaboration of what you have in mind in regard to (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >a</hi>) the taking by Japan simultaneously of an initiative, referred to in
                    numbered paragraph 3 of your 561, and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) such
                    modifications as would tend to meet a modified situation, the concluding words
                    of your 563.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
